# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Group operator terms: use the operator structure {#group-operator-terms-use-the-operator-structure}"
msgstr "Mengelompokkan suku operator: manfaatkan struktur operator {#group-operator-terms-use-the-operator-structure}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A [`BosonOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator\") can tag each of its terms with a **group index**. The tags carry no meaning of their own: they only say which terms belong together. What the tags *mean* is decided by whatever consumes them. In this package the consumers are the time-evolution gate, which is split into one factor per group, and the randomized qDRIFT pass, which samples whole groups.\n"
msgstr "Sebuah [`BosonOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator\") bisa menandai setiap sukunya dengan **indeks grup**. Tag itu tidak membawa makna sendiri: ia hanya menyatakan suku mana yang saling terkait. Apa *arti* tag itu ditentukan oleh apa pun yang memakainya. Dalam paket ini pemakainya adalah gate evolusi waktu, yang dibagi menjadi satu faktor per grup, dan pass qDRIFT acak, yang menyampel seluruh grup.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This guide shows how to assign groups, how to check the properties a consumer relies on, and how to lay the operator out so that picking a few groups out of a large one stays cheap.\n"
msgstr "Panduan ini menunjukkan cara menetapkan grup, cara memeriksa properti yang diandalkan pemakai, dan cara menata operator agar memilih beberapa grup dari yang besar tetap murah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  No automatic grouping strategy ships with this package. You assign the indices yourself, from what you know about your model.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Catatan\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Paket ini tidak menyertakan strategi pengelompokan otomatis. Kamu menetapkan indeksnya sendiri, berdasarkan apa yang kamu ketahui tentang modelmu.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Assign groups {#assign-groups}"
msgstr "Menetapkan grup {#assign-groups}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The running example is a three-site Bose-Hubbard chain. Each bond contributes a hopping pair, and the on-site interactions form a diagonal piece. The simplest way to build a grouped operator is [`from_terms_with_groups()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_terms_with_groups \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_terms_with_groups\"), which takes each term together with its group index as an `(actions, coefficient, group)` triple. You decide the group at the moment you write the term down, when you still know why it belongs there:\n"
msgstr "Contoh yang dipakai adalah rantai Bose-Hubbard tiga situs. Setiap bond menyumbang pasangan hopping, dan interaksi on-site membentuk bagian diagonal. Cara paling sederhana membangun operator berkelompok adalah [`from_terms_with_groups()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_terms_with_groups \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_terms_with_groups\"), yang menerima setiap suku bersama indeks grupnya sebagai triple `(actions, coefficient, group)`. Kamu menentukan grup saat menuliskan suku itu, ketika kamu masih tahu mengapa ia termasuk di sana:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The terms are stored in the order you give them, so the group indices cannot end up attached to the wrong terms.\n"
msgstr "Suku disimpan dalam urutan yang kamu berikan, sehingga indeks grup tidak mungkin terpasang pada suku yang salah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "An operator that already exists has to be grouped after the fact, by assigning the [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.groups \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.groups\") attribute. That is where care is needed, because [`from_dict()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_dict \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_dict\") does not specify the order in which it stores its terms. Writing the list out by position can then attach an index to the wrong term. Derive each index from the term itself instead:\n"
msgstr "Operator yang sudah ada harus dikelompokkan setelahnya, dengan menetapkan atribut [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.groups \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.groups\"). Di sinilah kehati-hatian diperlukan, karena [`from_dict()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_dict \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_dict\") tidak menentukan urutan penyimpanan sukunya. Menuliskan daftar berdasarkan posisi bisa memasang indeks pada suku yang salah. Turunkan setiap indeks dari sukunya sendiri sebagai gantinya:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The number of indices has to match the number of terms. Anything else is rejected, because a too-short list would silently drop trailing terms wherever terms are iterated together with their groups:\n"
msgstr "Jumlah indeks harus sama dengan jumlah suku. Selain itu ditolak, karena daftar yang terlalu pendek akan diam-diam menghilangkan suku di bagian akhir di mana pun suku diiterasi bersama grupnya:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check what the consumer relies on {#check-what-the-consumer-relies-on}"
msgstr "Periksa apa yang diandalkan pemakai {#check-what-the-consumer-relies-on}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Three functions in [`qiskit_bosons.operators.terms`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms#module-qiskit_bosons.operators.terms \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms\") answer one narrow question each about an existing grouping. None of them says a grouping is “correct”, because correctness is relative to the consumer.\n"
msgstr "Tiga fungsi di [`qiskit_bosons.operators.terms`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms#module-qiskit_bosons.operators.terms \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms\") masing-masing menjawab satu pertanyaan sempit tentang pengelompokan yang sudah ada. Tidak satu pun menyatakan pengelompokan itu “benar”, karena kebenaran bersifat relatif terhadap pemakainya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Is each group Hermitian?** This is the property that matters most. The time evolution of a group is only unitary if the group is Hermitian, and a lone hopping term $b^\\dagger_i b_j$ is *not*. Only the pair with its adjoint is Hermitian:\n"
msgstr "**Apakah setiap grup Hermitian?** Ini properti yang paling penting. Evolusi waktu sebuah grup hanya unitari jika grup itu Hermitian, dan satu suku hopping $b^\\dagger_i b_j$ *tidak* Hermitian. Hanya pasangan bersama adjoint-nya yang Hermitian:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A grouping that splits a hopping pair is caught immediately:\n"
msgstr "Pengelompokan yang memisahkan pasangan hopping langsung tertangkap:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The four hopping terms are caught. The three `True` entries are the on-site terms $b^\\dagger_i b^\\dagger_i b_i b_i$, which are Hermitian by themselves. A mode can legitimately repeat within a term, and nothing is dropped for doing so. The flags follow the order of `terms`, which is why each one can be read against the term it describes.\n"
msgstr "Keempat suku hopping tertangkap. Tiga entri `True` adalah suku on-site $b^\\dagger_i b^\\dagger_i b_i b_i$, yang Hermitian dengan sendirinya. Sebuah mode boleh saja berulang di dalam satu suku, dan tidak ada yang dibuang karenanya. Flag mengikuti urutan `terms`, makanya tiap flag bisa dibaca bersama suku yang dijelaskannya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Are the coefficients uniform?** A randomized product formula weighs a group by the mean *magnitude* of its coefficients, which is a faithful description of the group only if the magnitudes agree:\n"
msgstr "**Apakah koefisiennya seragam?** Product formula acak memberi bobot pada sebuah grup berdasarkan rata-rata *magnitudo* koefisiennya, yang hanya menggambarkan grup itu dengan setia kalau magnitudonya sama:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Neither check implies the other: uniform coefficients do not make a group Hermitian, and a Hermitian group can mix magnitudes. By default the magnitudes are compared, because that is what [`group_coeff_means()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms-group-coeff-means#qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.group_coeff_means \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.group_coeff_means\") averages. A Hermitian pair with complex coefficients has equal magnitudes but unequal coefficients, so it satisfies only the default form:\n"
msgstr "Kedua pengecekan ini tidak saling menyiratkan: koefisien yang seragam tidak membuat sebuah grup jadi Hermitian, dan grup Hermitian bisa saja punya magnitudo yang campur. Secara default, yang dibandingkan adalah magnitudonya, karena itulah yang dirata-ratakan oleh [`group_coeff_means()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms-group-coeff-means#qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.group_coeff_means \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.group_coeff_means\"). Pasangan Hermitian dengan koefisien kompleks punya magnitudo yang sama tapi koefisien yang tidak sama, jadi hanya memenuhi bentuk default:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  [`groups_are_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms-groups-are-hermitian#qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian\") is built on [`is_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.is_hermitian \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.is_hermitian\"), which compares an operator with its adjoint after normal ordering. That is an identity of the untruncated algebra, so a group that passes is Hermitian as a bosonic operator. See [Design principles of operator representations](operators#operators-explanation) for how products of ladder operators are ordered and compared.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Catatan\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  [`groups_are_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms-groups-are-hermitian#qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian\") dibangun di atas [`is_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.is_hermitian \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.is_hermitian\"), yang membandingkan sebuah operator dengan adjoin-nya setelah normal ordering. Itu adalah identitas dari aljabar yang tidak dipotong (untruncated), jadi grup yang lolos adalah Hermitian sebagai operator bosonik. Lihat [Prinsip desain representasi operator](operators#operators-explanation) untuk cara perkalian operator ladder diurutkan dan dibandingkan.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Order the terms by group {#order-the-terms-by-group}"
msgstr "Urutkan suku berdasarkan grup {#order-the-terms-by-group}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`split_out_groups()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.split_out_groups \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.split_out_groups\") returns one operator per requested group. When the terms of a group are scattered through the operator, it has to scan every term to find them. When each group forms one contiguous run, it binary-searches the group boundaries instead, so the cost of a lookup follows the number of groups *requested* rather than the number of terms *held*.\n"
msgstr "[`split_out_groups()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.split_out_groups \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.split_out_groups\") mengembalikan satu operator untuk tiap grup yang diminta. Kalau suku-suku sebuah grup tersebar di seluruh operator, fungsi ini harus memindai setiap suku untuk menemukannya. Kalau tiap grup membentuk satu rentang yang berurutan, fungsi ini melakukan pencarian biner pada batas-batas grup, jadi biaya satu pencarian mengikuti jumlah grup yang *diminta*, bukan jumlah suku yang *disimpan*.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`group_order()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms-group-order#qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.group_order \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.group_order\") produces that layout. It is a stable sort by group index: the value of the operator does not change, and terms within a group keep their relative order.\n"
msgstr "[`group_order()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms-group-order#qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.group_order \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.group_order\") menghasilkan tata letak itu. Fungsi ini melakukan pengurutan stabil berdasarkan indeks grup: nilai operator tidak berubah, dan suku-suku dalam satu grup tetap mempertahankan urutan relatifnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both layouts return the same operators; only the cost differs:\n"
msgstr "Kedua tata letak mengembalikan operator yang sama; hanya biayanya yang berbeda:\n"

